Subject: [PATCH 36/37] arm64: dts: rockchip: hand RK3588 decoders to MPP

Use the sole decoder compatible matched by the imported mpp_rkvdec2 driver and
add the vendor CCU/task metadata.  Linux v7.2's physical decoder addresses are
retained, including its corrected vdec1 fdc40000 window instead of the vendor
fdc48000 spelling.

The common MPP probe maps resource 0 as the decoder register base, while
mpp_rkvdec2_link.c requests the resource named "link" separately.  Therefore
the v7.2 function and cache windows are combined into the first "regs" resource
and the link window becomes the second resource.  Keeping mainline's original
link-first layout would map every decoder register from the wrong base.

Reference: armbian/linux-rockchip@fd9f82366e235b8afbdf516765210e97d24dce93:arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s.dtsi

Patches a file mainline already carries. The payload below is carried byte-for-byte from integration/0011-arm64-dts-rk3588-mpp-decoder-nodes.patch; scripts/build-series.py adds the mail header and nothing else, and scripts/verify-series-parity.py proves that independently.


